NAME
    wc - count lines, words, bytes

SYNOPSIS
    wc [-l] [-w] [-c] [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Counts lines/words/bytes of piped stdin, or a real file if <path> is
    given (walled to the project's own directory tree). With no flags,
    prints all three in that fixed order regardless of what order flags are
    given in, matching real wc.

EXAMPLES
    history | wc -l
    wc -l notes.txt
